"Evertec included in 2020 bloomberg gender-equality index","17332","today announced that it is one of 325 companies selected for the 2020 Bloomberg Gender-Equality Index (GEI) which distinguishes companies committed to transparency in gender reporting and advancing women’s equality.

Mac Schuessler, President and Chief Executive Officer stated, “We are proud to be included in the Bloomberg Gender Equality Index again this year. Evertec is committed to diversity and inclusion and we believe it is our formula for successful innovation. In addition, we are focused on recruiting, retaining and developing the highest quality workforce throughout our businesses in Puerto Rico and Latin America.”

The GEI tracks the financial performance of public companies committed to supporting gender equality through policy development, representation, and transparency. The reference index measures gender equality across five pillars: female leadership and talent pipeline, equal pay and gender pay parity, inclusive culture, sexual harassment policies, and pro-women brand. This year, Bloomberg expanded the eligibility for inclusion in the index to nearly 6,000 companies across 84 countries and regions.

""The 325 companies included in the 2020 GEI have shown their commitment to transparency and demonstrated leadership in gender-related data reporting,"" said Peter T. Grauer, Chairman of Bloomberg. ""Disclosure of company statistics and practices is an important first step in supporting gender equality globally.""

Through disclosure of gender-related metrics using the GEI framework, the firms included in the 2020 GEI have provided a comprehensive look at their investment in workplace gender equality and the communities in which they operate. Evertec was included in this year’s index for scoring at or above a global threshold established by Bloomberg to reflect a high level of disclosure and overall performance across the framework’s five pillars.

Both the framework and the GEI are voluntary and have no associated costs. The GEI is a reference index and is not for use as a financial benchmark. The index is not ranked. While all public companies are encouraged to disclose supplemental gender data for their company’s investment profile on the Bloomberg Terminal, those that have a market capitalization of USD1 billion are eligible for inclusion in the index. To learn more please visit the GEI website.","EVERTEC, Inc. (NYSE: EVTC) today announced that it is one of 325 companies selected for the 2020 Bloomberg Gender-Equality Index","2020-01-22 04:13:18","evertec-included-in-2020-bloomberg-gender-equality-index","djimenez","publish","https://dev.creativeteam.co/evertest/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/banner-Evertec-figura-en-el-indice-de-igualdad-de-genero-de-Bloomberg-2020-evertec.jpg","standard","closed","closed",,"wp-post","2.9.14","2.10.3","default",,,"a:3:{s:11:""text-editor"";a:3:{s:5:""count"";i:7;s:15:""control_percent"";i:0;s:8:""controls"";a:1:{s:7:""content"";a:1:{s:14:""section_editor"";a:1:{s:6:""editor"";i:7;}}}}s:6:""column"";a:3:{s:5:""count"";i:1;s:15:""control_percent"";i:0;s:8:""controls"";a:0:{}}s:7:""section"";a:3:{s:5:""count"";i:1;s:15:""control_percent"";i:0;s:8:""controls"";a:0:{}}}",,,,,"a:1:{s:18:""eael_ext_toc_title"";s:19:""Tabla de contenidos"";}","","banner-Evertec figura en el índice de igualdad de género de Bloomberg 2020-evertec",,,,"banner-Evertec-figura-en-el-indice-de-igualdad-de-genero-de-Bloomberg-2020-evertec.jpg","Noticias",,,"en","Evertec figura en el índice de igualdad de género de Bloomberg 2020","Evertec included in 2020 bloomberg gender-equality index",,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
"Ingenico Group and Evertec deploy Merchant Service Hub solution in Costa Rica and Panama","17338","Ingenico Group (Euronext: FR0000125346 - ING), the global leader in seamless payment and Evertec, a leader in payment processing in Latin America, jointly announce the launch of their Merchant Service Hub (MSH) in Costa Rica and Panama. This is the first time this solution will be available as SAAS (software as a service) in the north of Latin America region.

Ingenico Group and Evertec expanded their strong partnership to provide their clients with a fully integrated business intelligence solution including reporting and analytic services to complement their existing hardware solution.

&nbsp;

<strong>The solution</strong>

The Merchant Service Hub (“MSH”) will collect non-sensitive payment data from standalone POS, centralize all information and will provide merchants and estate owners with business intelligence services that will be available through a self-service, web portal. This solution is a web-based platform - flexible, scalable and designed with state-of-the-art big data technologies – that integrates seamlessly with the terminals increasing the value of the solution for estate owners. The Merchant Service Hub is available in Costa Rica, after a successful pilot deployed in various coffee shops in Panama.

&nbsp;

<strong>Improving customer knowledge, business performance and security for clients</strong>

The MSH aims at improving customer knowledge and business performance, by offering merchants a set of comprehensive and clear sales reports on daily basis. Merchants and estate owners can see and monitor their daily transactions and revenues, hourly performance metrics as well as clients’ average basket, providing them with specific sales KPIs and insights on their business activity.

Real-time monitoring and alerts together offer better store tracking and improved monitoring to detect any suspicious activity. Thanks to massive data querying and exporting capabilities, the solution improves internal accounting processes and facilitates business management providing merchants with simultaneous tracking of their stores.

&nbsp;

<strong>Enriching customer experience with a lighter environmental footprint</strong>

Thanks to our digital receipt service, the MSH solution has real environmental benefits. It helps to reduce paper waste production and carbon footprint up to 21 kg of CO<sub>2</sub>e per terminal and per year, ensuring compliance with current regulation on electronic invoicing in Costa Rica.

For <strong>Jose Antonio Pérez, Sales Director in North Cone of Latin America, Ingenico Group</strong>: <em>“The Merchant Service Hub is a unique solution, that offers a full set of integrated services with automatic reports, business intelligence and enhanced statistics for both acquirers and final costumers. Evertec has been Ingenico’s technological partner for a long time. Relying on our complementary know-hows, we are proud to provide our clients with one of the most sophisticated management tools in the payments industry. We are thrilled of this partnership with Evertec and thankful for their trust in our services, to help in timely decision-making in such a competitive market.”</em>","Evertec, líder en procesamiento de pagos en América Latina, e Ingenico Group (Euronext: FR0000125346 - ING), líder mundial en pagos seamless, anuncian en conjunto el lanzamiento de su Merchant Service Hub (MSH) en Costa Rica y Panamá.","2020-03-05 04:19:04","ingenico-group-and-evertec-deploy-merchant-service-hub-solution-in-costa-rica-and-panama","djimenez","publish","https://dev.creativeteam.co/evertest/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/banner-Evertec-e-Ingenico-Group-lanzan-Merchant-Service-Hub-en-Costa-Rica-y-Panama-evertec.jpg","standard","closed","closed",,"wp-post","2.9.14","2.10.3","default",,,"a:3:{s:11:""text-editor"";a:3:{s:5:""count"";i:6;s:15:""control_percent"";i:0;s:8:""controls"";a:1:{s:7:""content"";a:1:{s:14:""section_editor"";a:1:{s:6:""editor"";i:6;}}}}s:6:""column"";a:3:{s:5:""count"";i:1;s:15:""control_percent"";i:0;s:8:""controls"";a:0:{}}s:7:""section"";a:3:{s:5:""count"";i:1;s:15:""control_percent"";i:0;s:8:""controls"";a:0:{}}}",,,,,"a:1:{s:18:""eael_ext_toc_title"";s:19:""Tabla de contenidos"";}","","banner-Evertec-e-Ingenico-Group-lanzan-Merchant-Service-Hub-en-Costa-Rica-y-Panama-evertec",,,,"banner-Evertec-e-Ingenico-Group-lanzan-Merchant-Service-Hub-en-Costa-Rica-y-Panama-evertec.jpg","Noticias,Evertec en los medios",,,"en","Evertec e Ingenico Group lanzan 