"A volunteer day to remember","40757","<p>Volunteer Day is our annual day of community service. Once a year, from Puerto Rico all the way to Uruguay, we join efforts as a single Evertec team to carry out different activities to help make the world better for the families, environment, the animals, and the communities from where we operate.</p><p>This year, our volunteer campaign focused on diversity, and the event—held in November—embodied our commitment to society through multiple service projects. These projects were the result of the work of hundreds of our team members, who had the opportunity to share and support nonprofit organizations in Latin America, Puerto Rico and the Caribbean. Our excitement in bringing our diversity to the participants of the organizations we support was evident in the volunteer hours that were shared with these organizations. This, in turn, shows that our interest in supporting and collaborating with those in need is a genuine part of our corporate culture.</p><p>We are thankful for the support of our leaders and for the commitment demonstrated by those who organized and led our Volunteer Day. Thanks to them, we successfully placed Evertec volunteers in Chile, Colombia, Costa Rica, Mexico, Panama, Peru, Puerto Rico, the Dominican Republic, and Uruguay. A special thanks to the 22 organizations that welcomed us, making it possible for our collaboration in helping them transform the lives of children, the elderly, people with disabilities, and the animals they care for. We would also like to thank the organizations dedicated to protecting nature and our environment, a cause equally important for our organization.</p><p>During our eighth annual Volunteer Day, we provided support to the following organizations:</p><h4>In Puerto Rico</h4><hr /><ul><li>Instituto Loaiza Cordero</li><li>Fundación Síndrome Down</li><li>Siervas de Maria</li><li>El Comedor de la Kennedy</li><li>Hogar Ruth</li><li>Hogar del Niño Ave María</li><li>Hogar de Abu</li><li>Hogar Rafaela Ybarra</li><li>MDA</li><li>Brownie Blondie Foundation</li><li>Fundación Team 821, Inc., Vieques en Rescate</li><li>Programa REDES</li></ul><h4>In Latin America</h4>
<hr />
<ul>
 	<li>Hogar Bolívar</li>
 	<li>Fundación Planificable</li>
 	<li>Fundación Servidores del Servidor</li>
 	<li>Fundación Callejeros de la Misericordia</li>
 	<li>Fundación Orca</li>
 	<li>Corporación Masbosques</li>
 	<li>Fundación Bandera Blanca</li>
 	<li>Jompéame
Redalco</li>
 	<li>Karumbé</li>
 	<li>En busca de un hogar.</li>
</ul><p>There is still more work to be done. Our commitment is evident and the message is clear—at Evertec, we share common goals with these organizations: work in collaboration, provide aid, and focus on promoting social well-being. <strong>You are not alone. You have Evertec to help you move forward!</strong></p>","At Evertec, we are rich in diversity in terms of our gender, race, experience, ethnicity, education, generation, culture, age, nationality, and language. <b>But we are also rich in generosity. This was demonstrated through at our eighth annual Volunteer Day.</b>","2022-12-06 17:16:29","a-volunteer-day-to-remember","cmoya","publish","https://dev.creativeteam.co/evertest/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/voluntareado-2022.jpg","standard","open","open",,"wp-post","3.10.0","3.10.1","default","builder",,"a:3:{s:11:""text-editor"";a:3:{s:5:""count"";i:4;s:15:""control_percent"";i:0;s:8:""controls"";a:1:{s:7:""content"";a:1:{s:14:""section_editor"";a:1:{s:6:""editor"";i:4;}}}}s:6:""column"";a:3:{s:5:""count"";i:3;s:15:""control_percent"";i:0;s:8:""controls"";a:1:{s:6:""layout"";a:1:{s:6:""layout"";a:1:{s:12:""_inline_size"";i:3;}}}}s:7:""section"";a:3:{s:5:""count"";i:2;s:15:""control_percent"";i:0;s:8:""controls"";a:1:{s:6:""layout"";a:1:{s:17:""section_structure"";a:1:{s:9:""structure"";i:1;}}}}}",,,,,"a:1:{s:18:""eael_ext_toc_title"";s:19:""Tabla de contenidos"";}","","voluntareado-2022",,,"Voluntariado Evertec 2022","voluntareado-2022.jpg","Noticias",,"Optional","en","Un día del voluntariado para recordar","A volunteer day to remember",,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
"Evertec responds to the devastation caused by hurricane Fiona","40773","<p>This includes hurricanes like Fiona, which hit the Island of Enchantment in September of this year and after which a large portion of the western region is still struggling to recover. Aware of the impact, and as a demonstration of support toward the recovery efforts, Evertec in conjunction with ATH led an initiative where, from September 23 to October 7, Evertec matched each dollar donated through the “Donate” feature in the ATH Móvil application to 31 organizations that stood out for their work in helping those affected by the disaster. The maximum limit was set at $100,000 with a cap of $5,000 per organization, subject to the availability of funds.</p><p>According to Evertec President and CEO Mac Schuessler, “Hurricane Fiona inflicted hardship on Puerto Rico and the Caribbean, and our hearts go out to those affected. We remain deeply committed to the recovery and I am proud of our colleagues and their efforts to respond to these challenges.”</p><p><strong style=""color: #ff6c0c;"">Below, we have listed the institutions that were supported by Evertec and the citizens of Puerto Rico:</strong></p><ul><li>Taller Salud / TallerSalud</li><li>La Fondita de Jesús / LaFonditaDeJesus</li><li>Techos Pa' Mi Gente / TPMGCorp</li><li>Rehaciendo Comunidades con Esperanza / REHACE</li><li>MATRIA / ProyectoMatria</li><li>Casa Protegida Julia de Burgos / CasaJulia</li><li>Banco de Alimentos de PR / bancodealimentosdepr</li><li>Fundación Mochileando / FundacionMochileando</li><li>Ayuda Legal Puerto Rico / ayudalegalpuertorico</li><li>Fundacion Pisadas de Amor / FundacionPisadasDeAmor</li><li>Comedores Sociales de Puerto Rico / ComedoresSocialesPR</li><li>PlenitudPR / PlenitudPR</li><li>Puerto Rico Renace, Inc / PUERTORICORENACEINC</li><li>Red Por La Niñez /AlberguesPR</li><li>True Self Foundation / TrueSelf</li></ul><ul><li>Brownie Blondie Foundation / Brownieblondiefoundation</li><li>Scuba Dogs Society / Scubadogssociety</li><li>ConPRmetidos / ConPRmetidos</li><li>Centros Sor Isolina Ferre / CentrosSorIsolinaFerre</li><li>Fundación Yo no me quito / yonomequitopr</li><li>Para La Naturaleza /Paralanaturaleza</li><li>Hogar Forjadores de Esperanza / HogarForjadores</li><li>El Comedor de la Kennedy / ElComedordelaKennedy</li><li>Cáritas Puerto Rico / CaritasPR</li><li>Hogar Ruth / HogarRuthparaMujeres</li><li>Save a Sato / saveasato</li><li>Ciencia en Tus Manos / cienciaentusmanos</li><li>Iniciativa Comunitaria / IniciativaComunitaria</li><li>PRoTechos / PROTECHOS</li><li>Boys and Girls Club / BoysandGirlsClubsdePR</li><li>Cruz Roja Americana, Capítulo de Puerto Rico / CruzRojaPR</li></ul><h4 style=""text-align: center;"">Thank you to all who donated to show their support for this important initiative!</h4>","If anything has demonstrated Evertec's role as a corporate citizen, it is its immediate response to unexpected emergency situations that negatively affect our society. This is especially true when those situations happen in the countries where the company operates. One such example has been the various initiatives conducted in support of clients, collaborators, nonprofit organizations, and others affected by damages caused by the COVID-19 pandemic, which impacted the entire world, or the earthquakes and hurricanes in Puerto Rico.","2022-12-06 16:48:41","evertec-responds-to-the-devastation-caused-hurricane-fiona","cmoya","publish","https://dev.creativeteam.co/evertest/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/fiona-EN.jpg","standard","open","open",,"wp-post","3.10.0","3.10.1","default","builder",,"a:3:{s:11:""text-editor"";a:3:{s:5:""count"";i:4;s:15:""control_percent"";i:0;s:8:""controls"";a:2:{s:7:""content"";a:1:{s:14:""section_editor"";a:1:{s:6:""editor"";i:4;}}s:5:""style"";a:1:{s:13:""section_style"";a:1:{s:5:""align"";i:2;}}}}s:6:""column"";a:3:{s:5:""count"";i:4;s:15:""control_percent"";i:1;s:8:""controls"";a:2:{s:6:""layout"";a:1:{s:6:""layout"";a:1:{s:12:""_inline_size"";i