ls"";a:0:{}}}",,,,,"a:1:{s:18:""eael_ext_toc_title"";s:19:""Tabla de contenidos"";}","","retos y tendencias enfocadas al crecimiento y sostenibilidad de los negocios","retos y tendencias enfocadas al crecimiento y sostenibilidad de los negocios","retos y tendencias enfocadas al crecimiento y sostenibilidad de los negocios","retos y tendencias enfocadas al crecimiento y sostenibilidad de los negocios","retos-y-tendencias-enfocadas-al-crecimiento-y-sostenibilidad-de-los-negocios.jpg","Merchant (boletines)","automatización,billeteras digitales,digitalización,Evertec Colombia,inventarios,omnicanalidad,POS móvil,seguridad,sin contacto,tokenización,transformación digital","Opcional","es",,"¿Estas preparado para lo que viene en el 2024?",,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
"Are you ready for what's coming in 2024?","48055","<h2>Here are the trends for 2024:</h2>
<ul>
 	<li><b>Tokenization</b>
The security processes are advancing and the protection of sensitive data generated in transactions is important. The ""token"" is an alphanumeric value that is used to represent the original information without revealing it, it allows replacing credit or debit card numbers.</li>
 	<li><b>Digital Wallets</b>
It is essential to be able to provide your customers with the ability to store their debit and credit card information to streamline and facilitate the payment process for your products and/or services.</li>
 	<li><b>Omnichannel</b>
Merchants should strengthen the seamless and consistent shopping process across different channels to meet the needs of consumers who expect an integrated transactional experience.</li>
 	<li><b>Enhanced Security Measures</b>
As time goes by, data theft threats to merchants increase and for this also continuously improve technology to detect and stop fraud and/or unauthorized access quickly.</li>
 	<li><b>Inventory Management and Automation</b>
With the smart inventory management, you can easily view your current inventory levels, record inventory adjustments, create purchase orders, and even maintain a database of suppliers. This ensures that you have real-time visibility into your storage levels.</li>
 	<li><b>Mobile POS (mPOS)</b>
The use of smartphones and tablets as Point of Sale (POS) continues to grow.</li>
 	<li><b>Contactless Payments</b>
Your customers no longer have to enter their cards in a reader to make their payments. Contactless payments process the purchase intuitively, quickly and securely. Contactless payments also reduce the possibility of cloning fraud.</li>
</ul>
