"What's new in the PCI DSS v4.0?","57760","<h2>Some of the goals of these changes include:</h2>		
													<img width=""500"" height=""500"" src=""/evertest/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Seguridad.png"" alt="""" srcset=""/evertest/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Seguridad.png 500w, /wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Seguridad-300x300.png 300w, /wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Seguridad-150x150.png 150w"" sizes=""(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px"" />													
		<h5><strong>Continue to meet the security needs of the payments industry.</strong></h5><p><strong>Why it is important:</strong> Security practices must evolve as threats change.</p><p><strong>Examples:</strong></p><ul><li>Expanded multi-factor authentication requirements.</li><li>Updated password requirements.</li><li>New e-commerce and phishing requirements to address ongoing threats.</li></ul>		
													<img width=""500"" height=""500"" src=""/evertest/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Continuo.png"" alt="""" srcset=""/evertest/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Continuo.png 500w, /wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Continuo-300x300.png 300w, /wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Continuo-150x150.png 150w"" sizes=""(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px"" />													
		<h5><strong>Promote security as a continuous process.</strong></h5><p><strong>Why it is important:</strong> Criminals never sleep. Ongoing security is crucial to protect payment data.</p><p><strong>Examples:</strong></p><ul><li>Clearly assigned roles and responsibilities for each requirement.</li><li>Added guidance to help people better understand how to implement and maintain security.</li></ul>		
													<img width=""500"" height=""500"" src=""/evertest/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/flexibilidad.png"" alt="""" srcset=""/evertest/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/flexibilidad.png 500w, /wp-content/uploads/2024/02/flexibilidad-300x300.png 300w, /wp-content/uploads/2024/02/flexibilidad-150x150.png 150w"" sizes=""(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px"" />													
		<h5><strong>Increase flexibility for organizations using different methods to achieve security objectives.</strong></h5><p><strong>Why it is important:</strong> Increased flexibility allows more options to achieve a requirement's objective and supports payment technology innovation.</p><p><strong>Examples:</strong></p><ul><li>Allowance of group, shared, and generic accounts.</li><li>Targeted risk analyses empower organizations to establish frequencies for performing certain activities.</li><li>Customized approach, a new method to implement and validate PCI DSS requirements, provides another option for organizations using innovative methods to achieve security objectives.</li></ul>		
													<img width=""500"" height=""500"" src=""/evertest/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/procedimientos.png"" alt="""" srcset=""/evertest/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/procedimientos.png 500w, /wp-content/uploads/2024/02/procedimientos-300x300.png 300w, /wp-content/uploads/2024/02/procedimientos-150x150.png 150w"" sizes=""(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px"" />													
		<h5><strong>Enhance validation methods and procedures.</strong></h5><p><strong>Why it is important:</strong> Clear validation and reporting options support transparency and granularity.</p><p><strong>Example:</strong></p><ul><li>Increased alignment between information reported in a Report on Compliance or Self-Assessment Questionnaire and information summarized in an Attestation of Compliance.</li></ul>		
