"Watch out for hackers! Learn how to shield your business from the threat of cyberattacks","61339","<p>At Evertec, ensuring the security of your business, the transactions we process, and the services we provide is our top priority. Our mission is to provide you with the information you need to protect against malicious attacks.</p><p>To enhance the security of your payment processing systems, make sure to remember the following:</p><h2>Comply with<br /><strong>PCI DSS</strong></h2><hr /><p>The Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard (PCI DSS) is one of the first barriers to merchant protection. These technical and operational requirements help protect sensitive data from credit cards, debit cards, and other payment methods. PCI DSS compliance is a legal obligation for many businesses, significantly reducing the risk of a security breach.</p><h2>Tokenization<br /><strong>and encryption</strong></h2><hr /><p>Tokenization and encryption techniques are crucial for the protection of financial data. Tokenization replaces payment data with unique identifiers called tokens. Their advantage is that they are worthless if intercepted. On the other hand, encryption turns information into an unreadable format without a password. Both technologies prevent sensitive information from being exposed during the checkout process. Implementing both technologies can protect the business against cyberattacks and data breaches.</p><h2>Multi-Factor<br /><strong>Authentication (MFA)</strong></h2><hr /><p>Multi-factor authentication is a security measure that adds an extra layer of protection. Traditional authentication systems that only require a username and password are no longer enough. Unfortunately, cybercriminals use advanced methods to gain access to accounts. MFA in your payments system forces users to provide a second form of authentication, such as a verification code sent to their mobile device or biometric data, making unauthorized access difficult.</p><h2>Fraud detection<br /><strong>and prevention</strong></h2><hr /><p>At Evertec, we leverage our advanced technology software to monitor and prevent fraud on payment platforms. Analyzing unusual behavior, such as atypical purchases or multiple failed transaction attempts, is essential to detecting real-time fraud patterns. Investing in artificial intelligence enables businesses to detect threats before they can cause harm, helping them stay one step ahead of cybercriminals.</p><h2>Keep software <br /><strong>and systems up to date</strong></h2><hr /><p>Make sure to keep your payment platform systems and software updated. Cybercriminals are very sneaky and often exploit known vulnerabilities in outdated software to access systems and steal sensitive information. It's essential to have a regular update protocol and reliable security solutions in place.</p><h2>Staff <strong>training</strong></h2><hr /><p>Finally, the human factor remains one of the most significant vulnerabilities in any security system. Training employees to recognize phishing attempts, unusual behavior, and other potential threats is critical. Your team is the first line of defense against cyberattacks.</p><p>A proactive approach is crucial for earning customer trust and preventing expensive security breaches. Remember, safeguarding users' sensitive information is not just a legal obligation but also an investment in your business's reputation and future.</p><p><strong>References:</strong><br /><a href=""https://www.pcisecuritystandards.org/"">https://www.pcisecuritystandards.org/</a><br /><a href=""https://stripe.com/mx/resources/more/payment-tokenization-101"">https://stripe.com/mx/resources/more/payment-tokenization-101</a><br /><a href=""https://www.csoonline.com/article/3400367/mfa-security.html"">https://www.csoonline.com/article/3400367/mfa-security.html</a><br /><a href=""https://www.cybersecurity-insiders.com/payment-security/"">https://www.cybersecurity-insiders.com/payment-security/</a><br /><a href=""https://www.sans.org/security-awareness-training/"">https://www.sans.org/security-awareness-training/</a></p>","The digital ecosystem offers many tools that can significantly boost commercial competitiveness. While e-commerce provides many benefits, it's crucial to prioritize addressing cyber threats, especially in payment processing, to ensure continued success.","2024-10-07 19:39:08","watch-out-for-hackers-learn-how-to-shield-y-our-business-from-the-threat-of-cyberattacks","cmoya","publish","https://dev.creativeteam.co/evertest/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/ciberseguridad.jpg","standard","open","open",,"wp-post","3.25.10","3.25.4","default","builder",,"a:2:{s:11:""text-editor"";a:3:{s:5:""count"";i:2;s:15:""control_percent"";i:1;s:8:""controls"";a:2:{s:7:""content"";a:1:{s:14:""section_editor"";a:1:{s:6:""editor"";i:2;}}s:5:""style"";a:1:{s:13:""section_style"";a:4:{s:21:""typography_typography"";i:1;s:22:""typography_font_family"";i:1;s:20:""typography_font_size"";i:1;s:22:""typography_font_weight"";i:1;}}}}s:9:""container"";a:3:{s:5:""count"";i:1;s:15:""control_percent"";i:0;s:8:""controls"";a:0:{}}}",,,,,"a:1:{s:18:""eael_ext_toc_title"";s:19:""Tabla de contenidos"";}","","ciberseguridad",,,,"ciberseguridad.jpg","Merchant (boletines)",,"Optional","en","¡Ojo al pillo! Conoce cómo blindar tu negocio ante la amenaza de ciberataques","Watch out for hackers! Learn how to shield your business from the threat of cyberattacks",,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
"Cuestionario PCI: protege tus datos, tu negocio y tu reputación","61352","<h2>¿Por qué completar <br />el Cuestionario PCI?</h2><hr /><ol><li><strong>Compromiso con la seguridad:</strong><br />La razón principal para completar el Cuestionario PCI es proteger la información confidencial de los clientes. Los datos de tarjetas de pago pueden ser un blanco tentador para los ciberdelincuentes. Tus clientes deben tener la confianza de que sus datos confidenciales están protegidos.</li><li><strong>Evita multas y pérdidas:<br /></strong>Cumplir con los estándares PCI DSS no solo es una práctica recomendada, sino que en muchos casos es un requisito legal para procesar pagos con tarjetas de débito y crédito. El incumplimiento puede llevar a multas, sanciones y la pérdida de la capacidad para procesar pagos con tarjetas, lo que puede impactar las operaciones y rentabilidad de tu negocio.</li><li><strong>Mitigación de riesgos:</strong><br />Los altos costos directos asociados con la remediación de una brecha de seguridad, como la notificación de clientes y el ofrecimiento de servicios de monitoreo de crédito, también puede lastimar de forma significativa la reputación de tu organización. Cumplir con las normas del PCI DSS contribuye a reducir estos riesgos financieros.</li><li><strong>Protege tu reputación:</strong><br />Como sabes, los clientes valoran la seguridad de sus datos y, al demostrar que tu negocio cumple con los estándares PCI DSS, refuerza la confianza de tus clientes en tu empresa. La confianza del cliente no solo fomenta la lealtad, sino que también puede atraer prospectos que buscan seguridad en sus transacciones.</li></ol><h2>¿Cómo completar <br />el Cuestionario PCI?</h2><hr /><ul><li>Antes de completar el cuestionario: evalúa cómo se maneja la información de tus transacciones. Esto incluye revisar los sistemas de procesamiento de pagos, almacenamiento de datos y las políticas de seguridad.</li><li>Conoce los requisitos del PCI DSS: estos abarcan áreas como la protección de datos, la gestión de aspectos vulnerables, el control de acceso y el monitoreo de redes.</li><li>Responde el cuestionario: el Cuestionario PCI suele dividirse en secciones. Responde cada pregunta con precisión y ten a la mano los documentos requeridos para demostrar que estás en cumplimiento.</li><li>Implementación de mejoras: es posible que necesites llevar a cabo ajustes en tus prácticas de seguridad. Implementa las recomendaciones para atender cualquier área de no cumplimiento.</li></ul><p>El cumplimiento con PCI DSS no es un evento único, sino un proceso continuo. Asegúrate de revisar y actualizar regularmente sus prácticas de seguridad, no solo para garantizar el debido cumplimiento con las normas del PCI DSS, sino para tener la tranquilidad de que tus datos confidenciales y los de tus clientes están seguros. </p><p> </p><p>Referencias:<br /><a href=""https://www.pcidssguide.com/what-are-the-pci-compliance-fines-and-penalties/"">https://www.pcidssguide.com/what-are-the-pci-compliance-fines-and-penalties/</a><br /><a href=""https://securityboulevard.com/2022/06/what-are-the-consequences-of-a-data-breach/"">https://securityboulevard.com/2022/06/what-are-the-consequences-of-a-data-breach/</a>​<br /><a href=""https://www.techrepublic.com/article/pci-dss-compliance-improving-but-still-lags-highs/"">https://www.techrepublic.com/article/pci-dss-compliance-improving-but-still-lags-highs/</a><br /><a href=""https://smallbiztrends.com/what-is-pci-compliance/"">https://smallbiztrends.com/what-is-pci-compliance/</a><br /><a href=""https://www.pcisecuritystandards.org/"">https://www.pcisecuritystandards.org/</a></p>","El Cuestionario PCI es una herramienta establecida por el Estándar de Seguridad de Datos de la Industria de Tarjetas de Pago (PCI DSS, por sus siglas en inglés), un conjunto de regulaciones cuyo propósito es proteger los datos de tarjetas de crédito y débito. Este cuestionario es parte del proceso de cumplimiento de PCI DSS, que establece los requisitos de seguridad para cualquier entidad que acepte, procese, almacene o transmita información de tarjetas de pago.","2024-10-07 20:05:24","cuestionario-pci-protege-tus-datos-tu-negocio-y-tu-reputacion-2","cmoya","publish","https://dev.creativeteam.co/evertest/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/4-PCI.jpg","standard","open","open",,"wp-post","3.25.10","3.25.4","default","builder",,"a:2:{s:11:""text-editor"";a:3:{s:5:""count"";i:2;s:15:""control_percent"";i:2;s:8:""controls"";a:2:{s:7:""content"";a:1:{s:14:""section_editor"";a:1:{s:6:""editor"";i:2;}}s:5:""style"";a:1:{s:13:""section_style"";a:6:{s:21:""typography_typography"";i:1;s:22:""typography_font_family"";i:1;s:20:""typography_font_size"";i:1;s:22:""typography_font_weight"";i:1;s:22:""typography_line_height"";i:1;s:23:""typography_word_spacing"";i:1;}}}}s:9:""container"";a:3:{s:5:""count"";i:1;s:15:""control_percent"";i:0;s:8:""controls"";a:0:{}}}",,,,,"a:1:{s:18:""eael_ext_toc_title"";s:19:""Tabla de contenidos"";}","","PCI SSC",,"Protege La Información de tus clientes llenando el cuestionario de autoevaluación de PCI SSC",,"4-PCI.jpg","Merchant (boletines)",,"Opcional","es",,"Cuestionario PCI: protege tus datos, tu negocio y tu reputación",,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
"PCI Questionnaire: Protect Your Data, Your Business, and Your Reputation","61360","<h2>Why complete<br /><strong>the PCI Questionnaire?</strong></h2><hr /><ol><li><strong>Commitment to safety:</strong><br />The main reason for completing the PCI Questionnaire is to protect customers' sensitive information. Payment card details can be a tempting target for cybercriminals, and your customers need to have confidence that their sensitive data is protected.</li><li><strong>Avoid fines and losses:</strong><br />Complying with PCI DSS standards is not only a best practice but, in many cases, a legal requirement for processing debit and credit card payments. Failure to comply can lead to fines, penalties, and the loss of the ability to process card payments, which can impact your business's operations and profitability.</li><li><strong>Risk mitigation:<br /></strong>The high direct costs of remediating a security breach, such as notifying customers and offering credit monitoring services, can also significantly damage your organization's reputation. Complying with PCI DSS standards helps reduce these financial risks.</li><li><strong>Protect your reputation:</strong><br />As you know, customers value the security of their data, and by demonstrating that your business is PCI DSS compliant, you reinforce your customers' trust in your company. Customer trust not only fosters loyalty but can also attract new customers who are looking for security in their transactions.</li></ol><h2>How to complete<br /><strong>the PCI Questionnaire?</strong></h2><hr /><ul><li>Before completing the questionnaire: Evaluate how your transaction information is handled. This includes reviewing payment processing systems, data storage, and security policies.</li><li>Learn about the requirements of PCI DSS: these cover areas such as data protection, vulnerability management, access control, and network monitoring.</li><li>Take the quiz: The PCI Quiz is usually divided into sections. Answer each question accurately and have the required documents to prove you comply.</li><li>Implementing improvements: You may need to adjust your security practices. Implement recommendations to address any areas of non-compliance.</li></ul><p>PCI DSS compliance is not a one-time event but an ongoing process. Be sure to regularly review and update your security practices to ensure proper compliance with PCI DSS regulations and the safety of your and your customer's sensitive data. </p><p> </p><p>References:<br />
