"Protect Your Business: What to Do If Your Data Is Compromised","62998","<h2>What You Need<br />to Know?</h2><hr /><p>Any entity that suspects or confirms unauthorized access to, or misuse of, cardholder information—including those that store, process, or transmit cardholder data, or have access to payment systems—must follow certain key procedures. </p><h3>Essential Steps:</h3><h3>1. Containment and Control</h3><p>Act swiftly to limit the exposure of compromised data:</p><ul><li data-leveltext="""" data-font=""Symbol"" data-listid=""14"" data-list-defn-props=""{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}"" aria-setsize=""-1"" data-aria-posinset=""1"" data-aria-level=""1"">isolate the affected systems. </li></ul><ul><li data-leveltext="""" data-font=""Symbol"" data-listid=""14"" data-list-defn-props=""{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}"" aria-setsize=""-1"" data-aria-posinset=""2"" data-aria-level=""1"">preserve all evidence to facilitate the investigation. </li></ul><h3><br />2. Notify Visa and Mastercard Immediately</h3><p>Report the security incident: </p><ul><li data-leveltext="""" data-font=""Symbol"" data-listid=""15"" data-list-defn-props=""{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}"" aria-setsize=""-1"" data-aria-posinset=""1"" data-aria-level=""1""><b>Visa:</b> within three calendar days. </li></ul><ul><li data-leveltext="""" data-font=""Symbol"" data-listid=""15"" data-list-defn-props=""{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}"" aria-setsize=""-1"" data-aria-posinset=""2"" data-aria-level=""1""><b>Mastercard:</b> immediately. </li></ul><p><br />Include in your notification: </p><ul><li data-leveltext="""" data-font=""Symbol"" data-listid=""16"" data-list-defn-props=""{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}"" aria-setsize=""-1"" data-aria-posinset=""1"" data-aria-level=""1"">sufficient evidence to reasonably suspect or confirm a security breach. </li></ul><ul><li data-leveltext="""" data-font=""Symbol"" data-listid=""16"" data-list-defn-props=""{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}"" aria-setsize=""-1"" data-aria-posinset=""2"" data-aria-level=""1"">key details of the incident. </li></ul><ul><li data-leveltext="""" data-font=""Symbol"" data-listid=""16"" data-list-defn-props=""{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}"" aria-setsize=""-1"" data-aria-posinset=""3"" data-aria-level=""1"">contact us to report the incident and receive guidance on the next steps. </li></ul><h3><br />3. Conduct an Initial Investigation</h3><p>Prepare a detailed report and submit it to Visa, Mastercard, and Evertec within three calendar days from the initial notification. </p><h3>4. Preserve Evidence</h3><p>Ensure all evidence remains intact to identify the root cause of the incident, aid in investigations, and protect system integrity. </p><h3>5. Independent Investigation</h3><p>Visa and Mastercard may require an independent investigation before or in place of a PCI forensic review. </p><ul><li data-leveltext="""" data-font=""Symbol"" data-listid=""17"" data-list-defn-props=""{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}"" aria-setsize=""-1"" data-aria-posinset=""1"" data-aria-level=""1"">The investigating entity must not have provided services to the affected organization within the past three years. </li></ul><ul><li data-leveltext="""" data-font=""Symbol"" data-listid=""17"" data-list-defn-props=""{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}"" aria-setsize=""-1"" data-aria-posinset=""2"" data-aria-level=""1"">Visa and Mastercard reserve the right to reject reports not meeting their standards. </li></ul><h3><br />6. Notify Other Parties Involved: </h3><p> </p><ul><li data-leveltext="""" data-font=""Symbol"" data-listid=""18"" data-list-defn-props=""{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}"" aria-setsize=""-1"" data-aria-posinset=""1"" data-aria-level=""1"">internal teams responsible for incident management and information security. </li></ul><ul><li data-leveltext="""" data-font=""Symbol"" data-listid=""18"" data-list-defn-props=""{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}"" aria-setsize=""-1"" data-aria-posinset=""2"" data-aria-level=""1"">manufacturers or integrators of devices (PED/POS), if applicable. </li></ul><ul><li data-leveltext="""" data-font=""Symbol"" data-listid=""18"" data-list-defn-props=""{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}"" aria-setsize=""-1"" data-aria-posinset=""3"" data-aria-level=""1"">legal advisory teams, especially if applicable laws require customer notification. </li></ul><ul><li data-leveltext="""" data-font=""Symbol"" data-listid=""18"" data-list-defn-props=""{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}"" aria-setsize=""-1"" data-aria-posinset=""4"" data-aria-level=""1"">local or federal authorities (e.g., DACO in Puerto Rico or the U.S. Secret Service Cyber Crimes Unit for incidents in the U.S.). </li></ul><ul><li data-leveltext="""" data-font=""Symbol"" data-listid=""18"" data-list-defn-props=""{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}"" aria-setsize=""-1"" data-aria-posinset=""5"" data-aria-level=""1"">any other relevant parties as required by applicable laws. </li></ul><h3><br />7. Remediation</h3><ul><li>Address the identified vulnerabilities. </li><li data-leveltext="""" data-font=""Symbol"" data-listid=""19"" data-list-defn-props=""{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}"" aria-setsize=""-1"" data-aria-posinset=""1"" data-aria-level=""1"">Update security protocols. </li></ul><ul><li data-leveltext="""" data-font=""Symbol"" data-listid=""19"" data-list-defn-props=""{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}"" aria-setsize=""-1"" data-aria-posinset=""2"" data-aria-level=""1"">Ensure compliance with PCI DSS. </li></ul><ul><li data-leveltext="""" data-font=""Symbol"" data-listid=""19"" data-list-defn-props=""{&quot;335552541&quot;:1,&quot;335559685&quot;:720,&quot;335559991&quot;:360,&quot;469769226&quot;:&quot;Symbol&quot;,&quot;469769242&quot;:[8226],&quot;469777803&quot;:&quot;left&quot;,&quot;469777804&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;469777815&quot;:&quot;hybridMultilevel&quot;}"" aria-setsize=""-1"" data-aria-posinset=""3"" data-aria-level=""1"">Submit final reports and findings to Visa, Mastercard, and the acquiring bank. </li></ul><h3><br />8. Monitoring and Follow-Up</h3><p>Implement continuous monitoring to prevent future security breaches and reinforce preventative measures. </p><p>At <b>Evertec</b>, we are committed to ensuring that our business partners comply with these requirements. <b>Contact us</b> to ensure your business is protected. </p>","Do you know what to do if your business data is compromised? Below, we provide a practical guide with the steps to follow in case of suspicion or confirmation of a security breach that could put credit card transaction information at risk. It is essential to comply with the requirements established for such incidents.","2025-03-03 12:36:00","protect-your-business-what-to-do-if-your-data-is-compromised","djimenez","publish","https://dev.creativeteam.co/evertest/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Protege-tu-negocio-¿qué-hacer-si-tus-datos-están-comprometidos-.jpg","standard","open","open",,"wp-post","3.25.10","3.25.4","default","builder",,"a:2:{s:11:""text-editor"";a:3:{s:5:""count"";i:1;s:15:""control_percent"";i:0;s:8:""controls"";a:2:{s:7:""content"";a:1:{s:14:""section_editor"";a:1:{s:6:""editor"";i:1;}}s:8:""advanced"";a:1:{s:18:""section_custom_css"";a:1:{s:10:""custom_css"";i:1;}}}}s:9:""container"";a:3:{s:5:""count"";i:1;s:15:""control_percent"";i:0;s:8:""controls"";a:0:{}}}",,,,,"a:1:{s:18:""eael_ext_toc_title"";s:19:""Tabla de contenidos"";}","","Protege-tu-negocio&#8211;¿qué-hacer-si-tus-datos-están-comprometidos-",,,,"Protege-tu-negocio-¿qué-hacer-si-tus-datos-están-comprometidos-.jpg","Merchant (boletines)",,"Optional","en","Protege tu negocio: ¿qué hacer si tus datos están comprometidos?","Protect Your Business: What to Do If Your Data Is Compromised",,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
"Legacy Systems vs. The Cloud: Who's Winning the Battle?","63001","<p>It’s no secret that modernizing technological infrastructure and migrating to the cloud is a necessity, not just an option, to maintain competitiveness in an increasingly digitized business environment. However, for organizations dependent on legacy systems, the process isn't straightforward.</p><p>Legacy systems are technologies or software applications that, although they may function adequately in daily operations, over time become obsolete or may even hinder business growth and innovation.</p><p>One obstacle these companies face in making the leap to modernization is the comfort and familiarity with existing systems. After years of stable operations, transitioning to a new infrastructure can seem risky.</p><p>The flip side of this resistance to change is that tech leaders struggle daily with the inability to perform routine tasks in a cloud operation: system integration, report generation and Business Intelligence usage, access to innovative solutions with artificial intelligence, creation of new functionalities, continuous software updates, and more.</p><p>Additionally, the economic investment and time required often discourage transformation, as organizations with legacy technology often handle large volumes of data and must comply with numerous regulations.</p><p>System modernization implies a significant, yet not necessarily abrupt, change. This opens the possibility of moving select parts of the workload to the cloud while maintaining some legacy systems until they are ready for transition. Existing applications can also be updated to make them cloud-compatible, or adopting cloud-native architectures can improve flexibility and scalability.</p><p>This highlights the importance of having a business ally with experience and expertise in cloud technology. For Evertec, the goal is clear: to offer our clients the necessary solutions and support to make this transition securely, efficiently, and effectively. The integration of Nubity into Evertec has been a key step in our mission to transform our clients' technological experience across the region.</p><h2>Benefits of cloud<br />migration with Evertec:</h2><hr /><h3>Scalability:</h3><p>Allows for rapid implementation of changes and scaling according to market demands.</p><h3>Cost:</h3><p>Eliminates the need for investment in expensive hardware and ongoing maintenance.</p><h3>Security:</h3><p>Cloud service providers handle security and system updates and have advanced measures like data encryption, controlled access, and continuous monitoring.</p><h3>Optimization:</h3><p>Access to innovative solutions such as Artificial Intelligence and advanced analytics to drive business growth.</p><h2>The path<br />to modernization</h2><hr /><p>Before embarking on migration, what initial steps should the company take and what should it focus on?</p><h3>Inventory:</h3><p>Migration requires an understanding of dependencies, integrations, and performance requirements. A comprehensive inventory of applications and data should be conducted to identify components that can be migrated, refactored, or replaced.</p><h3>Regulations:</h3><p>Digitalization and cloud migration involve high responsibility and data security management. Reviewing specific requirements and regulations mandated by governments and industries is essential before any implementation. Examples include GDPR, HIPAA, or PCI DSS standards.</p><h3>Incremental approach:</h3><p>After reviewing regulations, adopting a phased incremental approach is recommended. This involves evaluating current systems and business needs to develop a detailed migration strategy with clear objectives, timelines, and resource allocation. Prioritizing critical and high-value applications first allows for refining the process before moving to the next phases. Each client will have a distinct approach as there are no magic formulas.</p><h3>Monitoring and updates:</h3><p>A fundamental part of a successful transition includes incorporating monitoring and performance management tools to ensure systems operate optimally in their new environment. Continuous adjustments and optimizations should be made to maximize cloud investment value.</p><p>Implementing new tools implies not just technological changes but also cultural and organizational shifts. Involving and training teams and collaborators is crucial to ensure they can fully leverage new technological environments and capabilities. </p><p> Discover how Evertec can make this transition for you at <a style=""color: #ff6600;"" href=""mailto:SalesManagementEvertec@dev.creativeteam.co"" target=""_blank"" rel=""noreferrer noopener"">SalesManagementEvertec@dev.creativeteam.co</a>.</p>","Some companies are still lagging behind in the digital race. How is cloud migration handled in companies that heavily rely on legacy systems?","2025-03-03 12:45:59","legacy-systems-vs-the-cloud-whos-winning-the-battle","djimenez","publish","https://dev.creativeteam.co/evertest/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Sistemas-heredados-versus-la-nube-¿quién-está-ganando-la-batalla-.jpg","standard","open","open",,"wp-post","3.25.10","3.25.4","default","builder",,"a:2:{s:11:""text-editor"";a:3:{s:5:""count"";i:1;s:15:""control_percent"";i:0;s:8:""controls"";a:2:{s:7:""content"";a:1:{s:14:""section_editor"";a:1:{s:6:""editor"";i:1;}}s:8:""advanced"";a:1:{s:18:""section_custom_css"";a:1:{s:10:""custom_css"";i:1;}}}}s:9:""container"";a:3:{s:5:""count"";i:1;s:15:""control_percent"";i:0;s:8:""controls"";a:0:{}}}",,,,,"a:1:{s:18:""eael_ext_toc_title"";s:19:""Tabla de contenidos"";}","","Sistemas-heredados-versus-la-nube&#8211;¿quién-está-ganando-la-batalla-",,,,"Sistemas-heredados-versus-la-nube-¿quién-está-ganando-la-batalla-.jpg","Merchant (boletines)",,"Optional","en","Sistemas heredados versus la nube: ¿quién está ganando la batalla?","Legacy Systems vs. The Cloud: Who's Winning the Battle?",,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
